{"quiz": {"questions": [{"q": "Why did Michael Nielsen remove his textbook 'Neural Networks and Deep Learning' from the public domain?", "options": ["He believes the content has become technically obsolete.", "He fears superintelligence will accelerate the discovery of destructive technologies faster than society can adapt.", "He was pressured by frontier AI labs to restrict access to foundational knowledge.", "He is transitioning to a new career in government policy."], "answer": 1, "why": "Nielsen argues that superintelligence poses a risk by enabling the rapid creation of destructive technologies that outpace human institutional defenses."}, {"q": "What is a primary advantage of using sodium-ion batteries for stationary grid storage compared to lithium-ion?", "options": ["They offer significantly higher energy density for long-distance transport.", "They are lighter and more compact for residential use.", "They utilize abundant, inexpensive raw materials and allow for safer shipping at zero volts.", "They require less maintenance because they do not use aluminum current collectors."], "answer": 2, "why": "Sodium-ion batteries use abundant materials like sodium carbonate and allow for safer, fully discharged shipping due to their aluminum configuration."}, {"q": "What did the pilot study at Sweden's Mottagning Neuropsykiatri clinic reveal about adult ADHD and autism diagnoses?", "options": ["Most participants required higher levels of medication after reassessment.", "Approximately 80% of self-selected participants no longer met the diagnostic criteria.", "The clinic found that previous diagnoses were almost always accurate.", "The clinic decided to stop offering reassessments due to lack of demand."], "answer": 1, "why": "The pilot study of 72 participants found that 80% no longer met the criteria for their original ADHD or autism diagnoses when evaluated based on current functioning."}, {"q": "What does research suggest about 'covert consciousness' in comatose ICU patients?", "options": ["It is a rare phenomenon that typically leads to poor long-term outcomes.", "It is easily detected through standard physical examinations.", "It is present in roughly 25% of vegetative or minimally conscious patients and correlates with better recovery.", "It indicates that the patient is fully aware but physically incapable of any neural response."], "answer": 2, "why": "Studies show that about a quarter of such patients exhibit covert consciousness, which is associated with significantly better functional recovery."}, {"q": "According to the European Registry of Exonerations (EUREX), what is a key limitation of their current data on wrongful convictions?", "options": ["The database only tracks cases involving violent crimes.", "The actual number of wrongful convictions is likely much higher due to procedural hurdles and institutional resistance.", "The registry only includes cases from the last five years.", "The data is based on self-reporting from prisoners rather than official court records."], "answer": 1, "why": "The registry notes that their count is limited by strict requirements for official exoneration, masking a likely much higher prevalence of actual wrongful convictions."}], "ai": true}, "groups": {"groups": [{"name": "Coffee drinks", "words": ["LATTE", "MOCHA", "ESPRESSO", "CORTADO"]}, {"name": "Planets", "words": ["MARS", "VENUS", "SATURN", "MERCURY"]}, {"name": "Cell parts", "words": ["NUCLEUS", "RIBOSOME", "MEMBRANE", "VACUOLE"]}, {"name": "Rivers", "words": ["NILE", "AMAZON", "DANUBE", "THAMES"]}], "ai": false}, "hive": {"center": "H", "outer": ["C", "I", "D", "M", "O", "E"], "answers": ["CHEMO", "CHIC", "CHICO", "CHIME", "CHIMED", "CHOICE", "ECHO", "ECHOED", "HEED", "HEEDED", "HEMMED", "HIDE", "HOME", "HOMICIDE", "HOOCH", "HOOD", "HOODED", "HOODIE"], "pangrams": ["HOMICIDE"], "max": 83}, "cryptogram": {"cipher": "RKO QYOJGQK HFGVGH KGCKFGCKRQ KAY TGCGJ HMTOOT LMVQ MVJ QKGXRGVC JGMCVAQRGH HTGROTGM MTO XATHGVC M JOLMRO AV